    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "To add: Milk pieces (Andres Serrano, Wolfgang Laib, Karsten\nNicolai)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"An empty canvas, apparently really\nempty, that says nothing and is without significance. Almost dull,\nin fact. In reality, however, crammed with thousands of undertone\ntensions and full of expectancy. Slightly apprehensive lest it should\nbe outraged ... It can contain anything but cannot sustain everything\n... An empty canvas is a living wonder -- much more beautiful than\nmany pictures.\"",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Wassily Kandinsky",
      "links": []
    }
